# Garden Town County — agent follow-through

- Do **not** ask whether to commit, push, or redeploy when work is ready for Git/Render.
- After finishing a coherent change set, **commit and push to `main`** unless the user explicitly said not to.
- Keep commit messages short and focused on why.
- Do not commit unrelated noise (e.g. incidental `county_logo.png` binary churn) unless the user asked for that asset change.
- Version scheme: next is `1.18.12` already shipped; then `1.18.13` … `1.18.99`, then `1.19.00`, `1.19.01`, …
- Bump `pubspec.yaml` version on user-facing releases when shipping features/fixes.
